# Security Review

Apply before merging auth, API, payment, or user-input changes.

## When to Activate

- Authentication or authorization
- User input, file uploads, API endpoints
- Secrets, credentials, sensitive data
- Payment or third-party integrations

## Checklist

### 1. Secrets
- [ ] No hardcoded API keys, tokens, passwords
- [ ] Secrets in environment variables only
- [ ] `.env*` in `.gitignore`; no secrets in git history

### 2. Input Validation
- [ ] Schema validation (e.g. Zod) on all user input
- [ ] File uploads: size, MIME type, extension whitelist
- [ ] Generic error messages — no internal leaks

### 3. SQL Injection
- [ ] Parameterized queries / ORM — never string-concatenate SQL

### 4. Authentication & Authorization
- [ ] Tokens in httpOnly cookies (not `localStorage`)
- [ ] Authorization checks before sensitive operations
- [ ] RLS enabled where applicable (e.g. Supabase)

### 5. XSS
- [ ] Sanitize user HTML (e.g. DOMPurify)
- [ ] CSP headers configured

### 6. CSRF
- [ ] CSRF tokens on state-changing requests
- [ ] `SameSite=Strict` on cookies

### 7. Rate Limiting
- [ ] Limits on API endpoints; stricter on expensive ops

### 8. Sensitive Data Exposure
- [ ] No passwords/tokens in logs
- [ ] Generic errors to users; details in server logs only

### 9. Dependencies
- [ ] `npm audit` / equivalent clean; lockfile committed

## Security Test Patterns

```typescript
test('requires authentication', async () => {
  expect((await fetch('/api/protected')).status).toBe(401)
})
test('rejects invalid input', async () => {
  expect((await fetch('/api/users', { method: 'POST', body: '{}' })).status).toBe(400)
})
```

## Pre-Deploy Gate

Block deploy if any CRITICAL item fails: hardcoded secrets, SQL injection, missing auth on protected routes, unvalidated uploads.

